<!--Render Target Documentation — RendererPipeline
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.RendererPipeline-->
<rdoc:RendererPipeline xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Internal pipeline of each block renderer
  </is>
  <documentation>
    These steps belong to this target. They are not a framework-wide pipeline.
    Numbers 9-11 below match the historical SCAD reference notes in the compiler
    handbook; the rest are internal to the processors.

    MBOM Block
      Module Name Resolver — FQN to SCAD module name
      Import Resolver — FQN to use/include paths
      Property Renderer — MBOM properties to settings entries
      Expression Renderer — expression AST to SCAD expressions
      Assembly Pattern Mapper — semantic values to SCAD assembly calls
      Composition Renderer — compositions to nested mb_block() calls
        (ScadBlockProcessor only)
      Set Renderer — set to STEPS array plus view submodules
        (ScadSetProcessor only)
      Customizer Generator — properties to the OpenSCAD customizer section
      Source Map Generator — BML positions to SCAD positions (Source Map V3)
      ScadFile(s)

    Before dispatch, on a working copy (canonical BOM unchanged):

    9. Target Resolver — look up machineblocks-v3-scad. If the target cannot
       support a block baseType, emit a diagnostic for that block.
    10. expandDirectives() plus id resolution — expand bml:each, bml:if, and
        bml:with on the composition tree. Then evaluate id expressions, assign
        deterministic auto-ids to static unreferenced children that still lack
        an id, and compose nested paths (parentPartId::childPartId) for output.
        Auto-ids are not written back to the BomDocument.
    11. Block renderer dispatch — exact FQN, then baseType chain, then delegates.

    Renderers may call framework validation utilities during the pipeline.
    They choose Urmodell, a pragmatic fork, or further forks. They do not mutate
    the canonical document.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:FqnNaming" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:RendererPipeline>
